From 15608877684826207c2cde5027c718bda9199165 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:59:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mempool: add TigerBeetle chunked slab allocator for mapTx and
 mapNextTx

Replace individual ::operator new node allocations in CTxMemPool::mapTx (boost::multi_index_container) and CTxMemPool::mapNextTx (indirectmap) with a TigerBeetle-style ChunkedSlabAllocator<T, 16384> backed by contiguous slab chunks and an O(1) LIFO intrusive freelist.

- Add SlabArena, ChunkedSlabResource, and ChunkedSlabAllocator in src/support/allocators/chunked_slab.h, serving single-node (n == 1) allocations from 16,384-slot contiguous chunks + intrusive freelist while forwarding multi-element (n > 1) hash bucket arrays to aligned ::operator new.
- Add an optional Allocator template parameter (with automatic value_type rebinding) to indirectmap in src/indirectmap.h while preserving 100% source compatibility for 2-parameter callers.
- Wire ChunkedSlabAllocator into CTxMemPool::indexed_transaction_set (mapTx) and CTxMemPool::mapNextTx in src/txmempool.h, along with memusage::DynamicUsage overloads.
- Add mempool_slab_allocator_churn unit test in src/test/mempool_tests.cpp covering direct slab bump allocation, multi-chunk growth, LIFO freelist reuse, allocator rebinding, n > 1 fallback, and CTxMemPool churn.

Build-prerequisite maintenance:
- Retain the existing overlay, s5, lazy-snapshot and mempool-queue interfaces removed by 020 while their implementations/callers remain; retain prerequisite filter/fee headers and the optional batch-collector declaration.
- Define the avabatch inventory ID required by the original 012 implementation/tests (0x20000006), preserve it in GetKind, and map its command name.
- Remove the stale treasury lock annotation until its V2 treasury mutex exists; no runtime treasury code is changed.
- Declare the existing mempool-batch vote variant and visitors with their 012 definitions; defer the V2-only supply gate until its V2 supply API is present.
- Defer the V2-only disk reverse-peeling declaration from the L1 header until V2 types exist; no L1 implementation or caller exists for it.
- Reorder the V2 circulating-supply integration case to the V2 API introduction; it referenced absent SetV2BlockCirculatingSupplyForTest on L1.
- Compile the original Avalanche batch hashing helpers and define their avabatch wire command. Vendor/link BLAKE3 for the existing non-consensus batch-ID hash; L1 tagged hashes and block/transaction consensus hashes remain SHA-based.
- Keep one copy of the adaptive-epoch accessors and freeze API duplicated by 023.
- Restore the missing testrawtxbatch result-lambda binding and removeUnchecked transaction alias, and include declarations used by validation; these are compile repairs to existing expressions.
- Include the concrete disconnected-transaction type in its native test, and retain the 011 inventory expectations (50/25 ms, 2500 items/s, 350000 retained IDs) across stale 020 test literals.
- Keep the first copy of each preconsensus batch test; 023 appended duplicate BOOST test definitions already present in 012.
- Declare the overlay warm-state flag and helper used by 038, which were otherwise delayed until V2 integration. Keep one copy of the bulk-clear function appended a second time by 038; omit its V2-only input flag check while the transaction type remains legacy.
- Implement the 039 PeekCoin declaration and admission caller: one existing-cache lookup, nullptr for absent/spent entries, no backing-view access or cache mutation. No definition exists anywhere in the original stack; this is an explicit missing-implementation repair.

